# Office for Civil Rights Puts Texas on Notice.

**Authors:** Roach, Ronald

## Abstract
While Texas officials scramble to adopt race-neutral admissions and financial aid policies in the public higher education systems, the U.S. Department of Education Office of Civil Rights has opened an inquiry into system compliance with civil rights legislation. Texas is the only state that prohibits affirmative action in higher education policies. The letter from the office to Texas officials is attached. (MSE)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ542977

